# Frozen TLE snapshot, 2026-08-10 — THE "TRUTH" SET. DO NOT REGENERATE CASUALLY.
#
# The second half of the TLE_DRIFT_MISS model (#62). The 2026-08-07 snapshot is
# what the planner computed against; this one is where the satellites actually
# were when the acquisition was taken, as re-observed three days later.
#
# The drift between the two is REAL. Both are genuine Celestrak observations of
# the same nine spacecraft, so the separation is what tracking actually
# recorded — orbit determination updates, drag, and in a few cases a manoeuvre —
# rather than a perturbation invented to make a demo interesting.
#
# Measured separation when both are propagated to the same instant:
#
#   SENTINEL-1B     0.4 km   (90h old)   inside every swath
#   ICEYE-X4        1.5 km   (89h)       inside every swath
#   SENTINEL-1C     2.6 km   (90h)       outside SPOTLIGHT only
#   ICEYE-X5        5.4 km   (91h)       outside SPOTLIGHT only
#   ICEYE-X2        6.0 km   (90h)       outside SPOTLIGHT only
#   CAPELLA-13     29.1 km   (98h)       outside SPOTLIGHT and STRIPMAP
#   CAPELLA-11    192.3 km  (106h)       outside all three
#   SENTINEL-1A   223.8 km  (123h)       outside all three
#   CAPELLA-14    829.3 km  (146h)       outside all three
#
# Two properties fall out of that, and both are the point:
#
#   Separation grows with the age of the planning element set. The sub-6 km
#   cases are all ~90h old; every case past 98h is tens to hundreds of km.
#
#   Narrow swaths miss first. SPOTLIGHT's half-swath is 2.5 km, STRIPMAP's 15,
#   SCAN's 50 — so a stale element set costs you the high-resolution modes
#   before it costs you anything else. That is the physical consequence of
#   setting a staleness threshold too loosely, which is the whole reason
#   tle_epoch is tracked.
#
# An earlier attempt derived the "truth" set by rewriting this fixture's epoch
# field instead. That is not drift: shifting the epoch of an unchanged element
# set moves the satellite along its orbit by the epoch delta, and a 6-hour shift
# on a 95-minute orbit put it 700-13,000 km away — a different point on the
# orbit, not a drifted one. Measured before anything was built on it.
